    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηρόκομ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κομέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tending old age</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χήτει
				γηροκόμοιο</span> for want <i>of one to tend one's
			age</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				605
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃς δαίμων ἀντ᾽ ἐμέθεν ὤπασε
				γηροκόμους</span>, i.e. daughters, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				536
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Tomi</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χείρ γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.1335
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φροντίδες γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					5.85
				</span></i>
			: in later Prose (written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηρωκόμος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				1.13.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Decl.</u>
				49.25
			</span></i>.</div>
